[statement]
Over an installed set, apk solves the installed world together with the
request. `foo` needs `lib>=2`, so the installed `lib` 1.0 is upgraded to the
2.0 the repository offers; `a`, installed but in no world, is removed.

[repository]
P:lib
V:2.0-r0

P:foo
V:1.0-r0
D:lib>=2

[installed]
P:lib
V:1.0-r0

P:a
V:1.0-r0

[world]
lib

[request]
foo

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove a 1.0-r0
upgrade lib 1.0-r0 2.0-r0
install foo 1.0-r0
